  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "A partition of a set $X$ is a collection of non-empty subsets of $X$ where every element of $X$ is contained in *exactly* one subset. \n\nTo find the subset that goes in the blank, we must identify which elements of $X$ are not yet contained within any of the given subsets.\n\nLet's go through each element of $X$ and check:\n\n- $2\\in \\{2,4,8\\}\\,✓$\n\n- $4\\in \\{2,4,8\\}\\,✓$\n\n- $6\\in \\{6,12\\}\\,✓$\n\n- $8\\in \\{2,4,8\\}\\,✓$\n\n- $10\\in \\{10\\}\\,✓$\n\n- $12\\in \\{6,12\\}\\,✓$\n\n- $14$ does not belong to any of the given subsets $\\,\\times $\n\nThe element $14$ is not yet contained within any of the given subsets. Therefore, the subset that must go in the blank is $\\{14\\}.$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
